---
import ProviderPlaybookTemplate from '../components/ProviderPlaybookTemplate.astro';
const data = {
 "kind": "nameservers",
 "name": "cPanel (hosting)",
 "title": "How to Change Nameservers in cPanel (hosting)",
 "description": "Change nameservers in cPanel (hosting) step by step: where the setting lives, what values to enter, and the propagation window to expect.",
 "intro": "Nameserver changes are delegation changes: you're telling the internet which servers hold your domain's records. Here is exactly where cPanel (hosting) keeps that setting and what to expect.",
 "panel": "cPanel is the DNS host, not the registrar: to point a domain AT this hosting's nameservers, get the two NS values from your host (often ns1.hostdomain.com) and set them at the registrar.",
 "steps": [
  [
   "Get the host's nameservers",
   "Hosting welcome email or cPanel home, General Information: the shared/reseller nameservers."
  ],
  [
   "Set at the registrar",
   "Custom nameservers at the registrar to those NS values."
  ],
  [
   "Wait",
   "Host NS changes are standard delegation: minutes to 48 hours."
  ]
 ],
 "quirk": "Hosting providers often run cPanel AND the registrar role; changing nameservers at the host-registrar to their own defaults is usually a one-click preset.",
 "faqs": [
  [
   "Is cPanel DNS separate from my registrar?",
   "Yes: cPanel is hosting software. If your domain is registered elsewhere and pointed at the host's nameservers, cPanel's Zone Editor manages it."
  ],
  [
   "How long do DNS changes take in cPanel (hosting)?",
   "The provider serves new values quickly, but resolvers keep old answers until each record's TTL expires. Verify live values with the record lookup, then watch the propagation checker until resolvers agree."
  ],
  [
   "Where do I find cPanel (hosting)'s nameservers?",
   "This playbook's nameservers guide covers the exact location. They are the delegation pair your registrar must point at for {name} to be authoritative."
  ],
  [
   "Should I lower TTL before changing records in cPanel (hosting)?",
   "Yes, for anything planned: set TTL to 300 seconds at least one old-TTL cycle ahead, make the change, confirm propagation, then restore the TTL."
  ],
  [
   "Can I keep email with one provider and DNS in cPanel (hosting)?",
   "Yes: DNS host and mail provider are independent. Publish the mail provider's MX, SPF, DKIM, and DMARC records in {name}, and keep those records unproxied."
  ],
  [
   "Which records should every domain have?",
   "A (and ideally AAAA) for the website, MX plus SPF/DKIM/DMARC for mail, and CAA to restrict certificate issuance. Everything else is per-service."
  ]
 ],
 "related": [
  [
   "DNS record types reference",
   "/dns-records/"
  ],
  [
   "TTL explained",
   "/what-is-ttl-in-dns/"
  ]
 ]
};
---
<ProviderPlaybookTemplate data={data} />
